WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 6.6 · MEAL: Monitoring, Evaluation, Accountability & Learning
The MEAL plan and budget

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your MEAL plan is a short manual for your evidence, even if there are only one or two of you.

3
00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:27.022
A MEAL plan brings everything together: results, indicators, data collection, roles, timing, reviews, evaluation, feedback and reporting. It is the short operating manual for your evidence, with a budget to make it real.

4
00:00:27.422 --> 00:00:28.022
What the plan sets out

5
00:00:28.022 --> 00:00:38.611
Roles: Who collects, checks, analyses, reviews and reports, even if it is one person. For example: The founder collects and reviews; a co-founder checks the entries monthly.

6
00:00:38.611 --> 00:00:48.459
Calendar: When data is collected, reviewed, evaluated and reported over the year. For example: Sheets weekly, a review each quarter, an end-of-pilot review in June.

7
00:00:48.459 --> 00:01:00.989
Budget: What MEAL costs in money and time: printing, transport, translation, compensation, reviews. For example: Printing, bus fares for follow-up visits and four hours a month of founder time.

8
00:01:01.389 --> 00:01:01.989
Why it matters

9
00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:08.404
1. Hidden MEAL work piles up on top of everything else a founder does.

10
00:01:08.404 --> 00:01:14.078
2. Many funders accept a MEAL budget line if you include it.

11
00:01:14.078 --> 00:01:20.752
3. Written roles make it easy to hand over as you grow.

12
00:01:21.152 --> 00:01:21.752
Where it shows up

13
00:01:21.752 --> 00:01:27.796
1. Your first proposals: MEAL appears as a costed part of the work.

14
00:01:27.796 --> 00:01:32.730
2. Your budget: MEAL becomes a line, not an afterthought.

15
00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:40.144
3. Handing over: the first people who join read it and know their part.

16
00:01:40.544 --> 00:01:41.144
What to avoid

17
00:01:41.144 --> 00:01:45.707
A plan so long that nobody reads it.

18
00:01:45.707 --> 00:01:50.641
Leaving out your own time because it is unpaid.

19
00:01:50.641 --> 00:01:56.574
Adding MEAL costs after the budget is already agreed.

20
00:01:57.174 --> 00:01:58.974
You write the roles, calendar and budget for your first year.

21
00:01:58.974 --> 00:02:02.974
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

22
00:02:04.474 --> 00:02:07.574
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
